{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKNojayHHLgB77twnczz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The tests were most likely added with the `rare-aliens-drive` changeset, but I could not confirm the commit, PR or ticket. My tools here don't include commit history, and no ticket key appears in the code I searched.\n\n**What the tests pin down**\n\nThe fetch wrapper in `openmrsFetch` handles a non-2xx response in its auth-failure branch. When the status is in `redirectAuthFailure.errors` (401 here), it calls `clearHistory()` and then navigates to the first non-empty of: the configured `redirectAuthFailure.url`, the response's `Location` header, or the default `${openmrsSpaBase}/login`. Unless `rejectAuthFailure` is set, it then returns a never-settling promise, or a resolved one if `resolvePromise` is true (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts:225-243`).\n\nThe test file has these cases:\n- **401 with a `Location` header** (`auth-module challenge`): with `url: ''`, navigation goes to the header value `/module/authentication/login.form`. This covers the backend-module challenge path (`openmrs-fetch.test.ts:166-185`).\n- **401 with no `Location` header** (`genuine auth failure`): navigation goes to the default `${openmrsSpaBase}/login` (`openmrs-fetch.test.ts:197-214`).\n- **Session endpoint 2xx with a `Location` header**: navigation follows the header (`openmrs-fetch.test.ts:187-195`). This is the success-side redirect, not the 401 path.\n- Existing cases already covered the configured SPA login URL on 401 (`openmrs-fetch.test.ts:216-233`) and rejection with `rejectAuthFailure` (`openmrs-fetch.test.ts:235-243`).\n\nSo the premise is only partly right: the configured-URL path and the rejection path were already tested. The two new-looking cases are the `Location`-header redirect and the default-URL fallback.\n\n**Why coverage was added (inferred, not confirmed)**\n\nThe changeset `rare-aliens-drive.md` says `openmrsFetch()` was made to handle 401s and 403s on the session endpoint so the framework can process them. It also moved session tracking onto this path. The test titles suggest the tests were written to lock in that backend-challenge and genuine-failure behaviour. I did not find a changeset or commit message that says so directly.\n\n**Commit, PR and ticket**\n\nI could not identify these. The changeset carries no ticket key. The only ticket-style keys near this code are `OA-41 #1231` in a comment on the 204 logout redirect (`openmrs-fetch.ts:188`), which is a different behaviour.\n\nEvidence, best first:\n\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts:166-185\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts:197-214\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts:216-233\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts:235-243\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts:187-195\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts:1-39\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts:225-243\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts:181-195\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/config-schema.ts:3-3\n- openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/config-schema.ts:14-14\n- openmrs-esm-core/.changeset/rare-aliens-drive.md:9-13\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 166, \"endLine\": 185},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 197, \"endLine\": 214},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 216, \"endLine\": 233},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 235, \"end